{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Send the sickle</b> — by way of parable, for it is written that the Ammonites and Moabites destroyed the inhabitants of Mount Seir and devoted them to destruction, and afterward each killed his fellow, and there was no survivor." "<b>Trample</b> — its way is by way of parable, and it is called the Valley of Decision — for it was finished and decided upon them. And the one who explains Jehoshaphat as 'YHWH will judge them' — this is the way of derash, for according to the peshat it is correct that a place is called by the name of its maker, like Turi-Shaddai; only the honored Name is not called by the name of a man. Therefore I explained that Solomon in the Song of Songs is profane [i.e., the name is used in ordinary, non-sacred register]."], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "Reading 'a place is called by the name of its maker' (שם אדם = שם עושהו), following the logic that Jehoshaphat the king named the valley; the alternative derash reads the name as 'YHWH judges.' The final clause about Song of Songs seems to jump topics; translated hyper-literally as printed."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:48.257850895Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}